On Radix, mio waits with poll(2), and its poll back end drops an
interest once it has reported it, until the source is registered again
(mio's IoSource types do that when an operation would block). crossterm
reads the terminal and signal-hook drains its socket straight from the
file descriptors, so after the first keys nothing woke the event loop:
register both again each time they are reported.

